  "completed": [
    "Two immutable pure native-x86_64 cBPF candidates: bootstrap listener notifies all write/pwrite64 calls, and a separate closed final seal denies alternate data-write channels and policy replacement. Neither program alone constitutes the intended meter.",
    "Architecture, tagged x32 and historical x32 rejection precede dispatch. Restricted scalar arguments inspect full width; all-descriptor writes have no FD/count-based exemptions.",
    "Final seal denies vector/async/copy/splice/reflink/ioctl/truncation/shared-mapping/descriptor-import channels and unknown syscalls. clone3 receives a fixed ENOSYS refusal, with actual execution still denied; the finite legacy thread clone remains flag-restricted.",
    "The broker parses exact candidate notification frames, retaining only private ID/syscall/count fields, and reserves requested bytes before ID-validation or response callbacks. Full unsigned scalar counts cannot wrap or become FD-dependent exemptions.",
    "Zero-length requests consume notification capacity. Invalid IDs, duplicate notifications, callback ambiguity/cancellation, budget exhaustion, owner mismatch, reentry and deadline expiry terminally fail without refund or retry.",
    "Only aggregate snapshots and fixed error codes are retention-safe. Exception objects/tracebacks may retain private frame values and must never be persisted. Public installer/server remain unconditionally closed."
  ],
