  "remaining_native_adapter_work": [
    "Verify expanded Linux syscall/flag/notification ABI candidates against authenticated target headers and runtime; do not infer kernel acceptance from the local interpreter.",
    "Bind and transfer exactly one listener during trusted bootstrap, install/read back both filters, close listener authority in the worker, and seal all transport/policy-replacement paths before payload release.",
    "Connect kernel notification ID-validation and response transmission to the precharge core, with terminal retirement of the owned workload on every ambiguity or failure.",
    "Keep independently armed parent-loss/deadline protection while servicing notifications; poll readiness alone does not prove cancellation-race RECV cannot block.",
    "Preserve RLIMIT_CORE=0, excluded inherited writable shared mappings/I/O authority, separate sparse-file/capacity bounds, and explicit setup/metadata/OS/scratch/report accounting.",
    "Finish existing dispatcher/lifecycle integration and authenticate the successor source closure before bounded Linux qualification and unchanged host/input/resource/real-import admission."
  ],
